  "acceptance_rules": [
    "A period (default this month, at most 366 days): reactions, wastage and component usage as percentages with their counts, the turnaround of issue by urgency; '-' when nothing was transfused, never 0 %.",
    "Trace a unit: pick it from GET /blood/units?status=Transfused (or Discarded, ReturnedToSource; newest first, continue with the last unit_id as before_id; without status it lists the units still on the shelf, reserved or out on a ward); GET /blood/units/{unit_id} gives each issue's transfusion_id, GET /blood/transfusions/{transfusion_id} its observations and reaction_report (reaction_id, incident_id).",
    "Registers name patients: say above the buttons that each patient printed is logged as a read of their record.",
    "A reaction: link to its incident (the analysis and the actions live there); the blood bank in charge (blood.bank.manage) adds the regrouping and the date and reference of the Authority's notice, each once (BLOOD_REACTION_RECORDED).",
    "Exists for the service blood_transfusion (records): show it as GET /establishment views.screens says for screen_id blood_registers (full; open_work: without its new work, with the banner \"No new ... from now on\"; records: history and corrections only; setup: only from Facility settings; hidden: in no menu), after login and again on establishment.changed. Never decide it from the profile's category."
  ],
